# Yuztoo website SEO (mandatory)

"Website" = the public Yuztoo site on this branch (`https://yuztoo.com`, local
`http://localhost:3001/`). It is isolated from the Flutter app and the CRM; never import their
code into it.

Whenever you add or change anything on the website (page, section, URL, image, content):

1. Do the full SEO in the same change, without being asked: follow
   `docs/holy-books/SEO_HOLY_BOOK.md` §0–§7 — SEO data module, prerender, sitemap, redirects,
   exactly one `h1`, JSON-LD, local images with French `alt`.
2. Update `docs/holy-books/SEO_HOLY_BOOK.md`: §9 Page registry, §10 Changelog (dated line), and
   §8 Known gaps when one is closed or found.
3. Run `npm run build` — it must end with `✓ SEO gate: … all checks passed`
   (`scripts/verify-seo.mjs`). Fix the page, never loosen the gate.
4. Any form: follow SEO_HOLY_BOOK §11 — `source = "Site web / <Page>"`, the server-side allowlist
   in the Cloud Function, honeypot, consent link to `/confidentialite`.
5. Renamed or removed URL: add a 301 to `firebase.json` `redirects` in the same change.
6. Deploy to **both** `yuztoo-dev` and `yuztoo` (see the `firebase-dual-env-deploy` rule). Never
   deploy one environment and stop.
